 ],
 "balloons": [
  {
   "panel": "page-01-panel-02",
   "balloon": 1,
   "speakers": [
    "BOY (from above)"
   ],
   "text": "Three ships. No, four. The new one is smaller.",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": []
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-01-panel-03",
   "balloon": 1,
   "speakers": [
    "GUARD"
   ],
   "text": "The banded flag?",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": [
    "ibrahim",
    "nagoji",
    "kayal"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-01-panel-03",
   "balloon": 2,
   "speakers": [
    "BOY (from above)"
   ],
   "text": "Red, white, blue.",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": [
    "ibrahim",
    "nagoji",
    "kayal"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-01-panel-04",
   "balloon": 1,
   "speakers": [
    "GUARD"
   ],
   "text": "Company ships. Dutch.",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": [
    "nagoji",
    "kayal"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-02-panel-01",
   "balloon": 1,
   "speakers": [
    "BOY"
   ],
   "text": "They are closer than yesterday.",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": []
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-02-panel-01",
   "balloon": 2,
   "speakers": [
    "BOY"
   ],
   "text": "These ones move like men who know where they are going.",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": []
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-02-panel-02",
   "balloon": 1,
   "speakers": [
    "NAGOJI"
   ],
   "text": "And who leads them?",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": [
    "nagoji",
    "kayal"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-02-panel-02",
   "balloon": 2,
   "speakers": [
    "BOY (from above)"
   ],
   "text": "The same tall captain. The one with the pale hair and the stick he uses to beat his men into straight lines.",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": [
    "nagoji",
    "kayal"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-02-panel-03",
   "balloon": 1,
   "speakers": [
    "GUARD (off)"
   ],
   "text": "He drills them until they piss in step.",
   "tail": "tail to the panel edge (off-panel speaker)",
   "cast": [
    "eustachius"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-02-panel-03",
   "balloon": 2,
   "speakers": [
    "BOY (off)"
   ],
   "text": "When he turns, the men move. When he scratches his nose, they move slower.",
   "tail": "tail to the panel edge (off-panel speaker)",
   "cast": [
    "eustachius"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-02-panel-04",
   "balloon": 1,
   "speakers": [
    "NAGOJI"
   ],
   "text": "Keep watching. Count how many days they hover. Count how close they dare come.",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": [
    "nagoji",
    "kayal"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-02-panel-05",
   "balloon": 1,
   "speakers": [
    "IBRAHIM"
   ],
   "text": "They smell blood. Or pepper. To them it is the same.",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": [
    "ibrahim",
    "nagoji",
    "kayal"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-02-panel-05",
   "balloon": 2,
   "speakers": [
    "NAGOJI"
   ],
   "text": "They smell a king who does not kneel easily.",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": [
    "ibrahim",
    "nagoji",
    "kayal"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-02-panel-05",
   "balloon": 3,
   "speakers": [
    "IBRAHIM"
   ],
   "text": "That too.",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": [
    "ibrahim",
    "nagoji",
    "kayal"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-03-panel-01",
   "balloon": 1,
   "speakers": [
    "VARMA (not looking up)"
   ],
   "text": "Sawant. Tell me.",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": [
    "ibrahim",
    "nagoji",
    "ramayyan",
    "varma"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-03-panel-02",
   "balloon": 1,
   "speakers": [
    "NAGOJI"
   ],
   "text": "Four company ships. Three large, one smaller. Moving south.",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": [
    "nagoji"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-03-panel-02",
   "balloon": 2,
   "speakers": [
    "NAGOJI"
   ],
   "text": "The same tall officer on the quarterdeck. Pale hair, stiff back. He drills them hard.",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": [
    "nagoji"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-03-panel-03",
   "balloon": 1,
   "speakers": [
    "RAMAYYAN"
   ],
   "text": "Here. If they hold that course and that speed.",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": [
    "ramayyan"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-03-panel-04",
   "balloon": 1,
   "speakers": [
    "IBRAHIM"
   ],
   "text": "They will anchor within sight of our coast by evening. Close enough to send boats ashore.",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": [
    "ibrahim"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-03-panel-04",
   "balloon": 2,
   "speakers": [
    "IBRAHIM"
   ],
   "text": "Gifts for those who fear you more than the company. Promises written in thick ink and broken in thin whispers.",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": [
    "ibrahim"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-03-panel-05",
   "balloon": 1,
   "speakers": [
    "VARMA"
   ],
   "text": "They test us. They want to see how high we raise our hackles when they show their teeth.",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": [
    "varma"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-03-panel-05",
   "balloon": 2,
   "speakers": [
    "VARMA"
   ],
   "text": "What would your Peshwa do?",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": [
    "varma"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-04-panel-01",
   "balloon": 1,
   "speakers": [
    "NAGOJI"
   ],
   "text": "He would send letters. But he would not move his own men until he had counted the cost twice.",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": [
    "nagoji"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-04-panel-01",
   "balloon": 2,
   "speakers": [
    "NAGOJI"
   ],
   "text": "His coast is not as tightly bound to his capital as yours is. He can afford to pretend distance.",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": [
    "nagoji"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-04-panel-02",
   "balloon": 1,
   "speakers": [
    "VARMA"
   ],
   "text": "I cannot. If the Dutch piss in our waters, the smell reaches my throne the same day.",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": [
    "varma"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-04-panel-03",
   "balloon": 1,
   "speakers": [
    "RAMAYYAN"
   ],
   "text": "These ships answer to the Zeeland chamber of the company.",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": [
    "ramayyan"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-04-panel-03",
   "balloon": 2,
   "speakers": [
    "RAMAYYAN"
   ],
   "text": "Their commander is cautioned not to provoke open war. Only to remind local chiefs who controls trade. He will test alliances.",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": [
    "ramayyan"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-04-panel-03",
   "balloon": 3,
   "speakers": [
    "NAGOJI (off)"
   ],
   "text": "And our sand drills? What do they make of those?",
   "tail": "tail to the panel edge (off-panel speaker)",
   "cast": [
    "ramayyan"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-04-panel-04",
   "balloon": 1,
   "speakers": [
    "VARMA (off)"
   ],
   "text": "I want them to glimpse enough to worry.",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": [
    "varma"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-04-panel-04",
   "balloon": 2,
   "speakers": [
    "VARMA (off)"
   ],
   "text": "Not enough to understand.",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": [
    "varma"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-04-panel-05",
   "balloon": 1,
   "speakers": [
    "VARMA"
   ],
   "text": "I have not forgotten what you did in February.",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": [
    "varma"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-05-panel-02",
   "balloon": 1,
   "speakers": [
    "RAMAYYAN (whisper)"
   ],
   "text": "Let Van Imhoff wonder whether the Peshwa's men ride south for pepper or for alliance.",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": [
    "dhanaji",
    "nagoji",
    "ramayyan",
    "varma"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-05-panel-02",
   "balloon": 2,
   "speakers": [
    "RAMAYYAN (whisper)"
   ],
   "text": "A question he cannot answer is worth more than a hundred soldiers he can count.",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": [
    "dhanaji",
    "nagoji",
    "ramayyan",
    "varma"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-06-panel-02",
   "balloon": 1,
   "speakers": [
    "VARMA"
   ],
   "text": "One thousand kalanjus. For the hiranyagarbha ceremony.",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": [
    "varma"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-06-panel-02",
   "balloon": 2,
   "speakers": [
    "VARMA"
   ],
   "text": "A gesture of friendship from the Company.",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": [
    "varma"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-06-panel-04",
   "balloon": 1,
   "speakers": [
    "VAN IMHOFF"
   ],
   "text": "Eight.",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": [
    "van_imhoff"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-07-panel-01",
   "balloon": 1,
   "speakers": [
    "VARMA"
   ],
   "text": "Take a small party of riders along the coast. In sight of their ships, out of cannon range.",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": [
    "varma"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-07-panel-01",
   "balloon": 2,
   "speakers": [
    "VARMA"
   ],
   "text": "Let their glass see horse that do not fear the water's edge.",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": [
    "varma"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-07-panel-02",
   "balloon": 1,
   "speakers": [
    "NAGOJI"
   ],
   "text": "They will think we mean to charge the sea.",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": [
    "nagoji"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-07-panel-03",
   "balloon": 1,
   "speakers": [
    "VARMA"
   ],
   "text": "Let them think many things. Confusion is a useful ally.",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": [
    "varma"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-07-panel-03",
   "balloon": 2,
   "speakers": [
    "VARMA"
   ],
   "text": "We will not fire first. But we will not lower our heads either.",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": [
    "varma"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-07-panel-04",
   "balloon": 1,
   "speakers": [
    "RAMAYYAN"
   ],
   "text": "Our men on the backwaters will count their boats. Our scribes in the markets will listen.",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": [
    "ramayyan"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-07-panel-04",
   "balloon": 2,
   "speakers": [
    "RAMAYYAN"
   ],
   "text": "Our temple men will note which sleeves carry new gold.",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": [
    "ramayyan"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-08-panel-04",
   "balloon": 1,
   "speakers": [
    "ENVOY"
   ],
   "text": "Maharaja. The Honourable Company brings greetings, and hopes for continued friendship.",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": [
    "dutch_envoys",
    "varma"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-08-panel-04",
   "balloon": 2,
   "speakers": [
    "VARMA"
   ],
   "text": "You bring ships that sit like crows on our water. Is that how your company shows friendship?",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": [
    "dutch_envoys",
    "varma"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-09-panel-01",
   "balloon": 1,
   "speakers": [
    "ENVOY"
   ],
   "text": "Our ships patrol the coast to protect trade. There are pirates.",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": [
    "dutch_envoys"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-09-panel-01",
   "balloon": 2,
   "speakers": [
    "ENVOY"
   ],
   "text": "The seas are not as peaceful as we would like.",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": [
    "dutch_envoys"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-09-panel-02",
   "balloon": 1,
   "speakers": [
    "VARMA"
   ],
   "text": "Nor is the land.",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": [
    "varma"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-09-panel-02",
   "balloon": 2,
   "speakers": [
    "VARMA"
   ],
   "text": "Yet you do not see my horse standing in your streets in Batavia.",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": [
    "varma"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-10-panel-01",
   "balloon": 1,
   "speakers": [
    "ENVOY"
   ],
   "text": "We wish only to reaffirm our treaties with the important houses of this coast.",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": [
    "dutch_envoys"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-10-panel-02",
   "balloon": 1,
   "speakers": [
    "REVATHI"
   ],
   "text": "Our treaties stand. They say nothing of the company telling my kin in Travancore how many muskets to buy, or whom to marry.",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": [
    "revathi"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-10-panel-03",
   "balloon": 1,
   "speakers": [
    "ENVOY"
   ],
   "text": "Princess. We know the history of your line. We come with renewed respect.",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": [
    "dutch_envoys"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-11-panel-01",
   "balloon": 1,
   "speakers": [
    "REVATHI"
   ],
   "text": "Respect is shown in actions, not words.",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": [
    "dutch_envoys",
    "revathi"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-11-panel-01",
   "balloon": 2,
   "speakers": [
    "REVATHI"
   ],
   "text": "Last time your company men came to Velinadu with arrogance, many of them fed the earth. We have not forgotten. I doubt their widows have either.",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": [
    "dutch_envoys",
    "revathi"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-11-panel-02",
   "balloon": 1,
   "speakers": [
    "ENVOY (off)"
   ],
   "text": "Those events belonged to another time. Another management.",
   "tail": "tail to the panel edge (off-panel speaker)",
   "cast": [
    "revathi"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-11-panel-02",
   "balloon": 2,
   "speakers": [
    "REVATHI"
   ],
   "text": "Our memories do not change when your clerk's handwriting does.",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": [
    "revathi"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-12-panel-01",
   "balloon": 1,
   "speakers": [
    "VARMA"
   ],
   "text": "We are not here to relive old mistakes. We are here to see whether new ones can be avoided.",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": [
    "varma"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-12-panel-02",
   "balloon": 1,
   "speakers": [
    "VARMA (off)"
   ],
   "text": "You owe tax to my throne, promises to Velinadu and oaths to the Dutch. That is a great many directions for your heads to bow.",
   "tail": "tail to the panel edge (off-panel speaker)",
   "cast": []
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-12-panel-03",
   "balloon": 1,
   "speakers": [
    "CHIEF WITH HAIR STICK"
   ],
   "text": "We are pulled like rope in a tug of war. We wish only that the rope not break.",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": []
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-13-panel-01",
   "balloon": 1,
   "speakers": [
    "RAMAYYAN"
   ],
   "text": "Rope breaks when it is worn or rotten.",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": [
    "ibrahim",
    "ramayyan"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-13-panel-01",
   "balloon": 2,
   "speakers": [
    "RAMAYYAN"
   ],
   "text": "Would you rather be tied to a king who lives among you, or to a company whose masters sit beyond the sea?",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": [
    "ibrahim",
    "ramayyan"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-13-panel-02",
   "balloon": 1,
   "speakers": [
    "CHIEF IN GOLD CHAINS"
   ],
   "text": "The company pays fair weight. Twelve varahans the candi, in good gold pagodas.",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": [
    "padmini"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-13-panel-02",
   "balloon": 2,
   "speakers": [
    "PADMINI"
   ],
   "text": "Fair weight. And then they sell that pepper at three times the price elsewhere. Ask them what is fair.",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": [
    "padmini"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-14-panel-01",
   "balloon": 1,
   "speakers": [
    "CHIEF IN WHITE"
   ],
   "text": "What of Kottarakkara?",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": []
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-14-panel-01",
   "balloon": 2,
   "speakers": [
    "CHIEF IN WHITE"
   ],
   "text": "The Elayadathu chief still receives Dutch factors. His sister's daughter writes to Velinadu. There are whispers.",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": []
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-14-panel-04",
   "balloon": 1,
   "speakers": [
    "VARMA"
   ],
   "text": "Kottarakkara will be addressed in its time.",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": [
    "varma"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-14-panel-04",
   "balloon": 2,
   "speakers": [
    "VARMA"
   ],
   "text": "We are not here to discuss houses that have not yet learned to count.",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": [
    "varma"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-15-panel-01",
   "balloon": 1,
   "speakers": [
    "VARMA"
   ],
   "text": "This land is not theirs. The roads are not theirs. The fields are not theirs.",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": [
    "dutch_envoys",
    "nagoji",
    "padmini",
    "revathi",
    "varma"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-15-panel-01",
   "balloon": 2,
   "speakers": [
    "VARMA"
   ],
   "text": "The men who die when guns fire are not theirs.",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": [
    "dutch_envoys",
    "nagoji",
    "padmini",
    "revathi",
    "varma"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-15-panel-02",
   "balloon": 1,
   "speakers": [
    "VARMA (off)"
   ],
   "text": "You will have your pepper. You will pay for it. You will build no new forts on this coast without my consent.",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": []
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-15-panel-02",
   "balloon": 2,
   "speakers": [
    "VARMA (off)"
   ],
   "text": "You will not arm my enemies.",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": []
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-16-panel-01",
   "balloon": 1,
   "speakers": [
    "VARMA"
   ],
   "text": "In return, your ships will be supplied, and your merchants safe from bandits who think Europeans make sound targets.",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": [
    "dutch_envoys",
    "varma"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-16-panel-01",
   "balloon": 2,
   "speakers": [
    "ENVOY"
   ],
   "text": "And if we refuse?",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": [
    "dutch_envoys",
    "varma"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-17-panel-01",
   "balloon": 1,
   "speakers": [
    "VARMA"
   ],
   "text": "Then you test our patience.",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": [
    "varma"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-17-panel-02",
   "balloon": 1,
   "speakers": [
    "VARMA"
   ],
   "text": "And our sand.",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": [
    "varma"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-17-panel-04",
   "balloon": 1,
   "speakers": [
    "ENVOY"
   ],
   "text": "We will convey your words to our superiors. Meanwhile, a written agreement, signed by you, the Velinadu house, and the leading landholders.",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": [
    "dutch_envoys"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-17-panel-05",
   "balloon": 1,
   "speakers": [
    "REVATHI"
   ],
   "text": "We will read every line. Twice.",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": [
    "ramayyan",
    "revathi"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-17-panel-05",
   "balloon": 2,
   "speakers": [
    "RAMAYYAN"
   ],
   "text": "And we will draft some of our own. Our scribes are not as slow as you may think.",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": [
    "ramayyan",
    "revathi"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-18-panel-03",
   "balloon": 1,
   "speakers": [
    "REVATHI"
   ],
   "text": "You have been very quiet, Sawant. Does all this talk bore a man who prefers the noise of hooves?",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": [
    "nagoji",
    "revathi"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-18-panel-04",
   "balloon": 1,
   "speakers": [
    "NAGOJI"
   ],
   "text": "On the contrary. I am learning how many ways there are to start wars without lifting a sword.",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": [
    "nagoji"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-18-panel-05",
   "balloon": 1,
   "speakers": [
    "REVATHI"
   ],
   "text": "Good. If you are to serve here, you must learn to hear when a word carries the weight of a musket.",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": [
    "revathi"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-18-panel-05",
   "balloon": 2,
   "speakers": [
    "REVATHI"
   ],
   "text": "Otherwise you will charge at the wrong time.",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": [
    "revathi"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-19-panel-01",
   "balloon": 1,
   "speakers": [
    "REVATHI"
   ],
   "text": "Two years ago he took Dutch coin to rebuild his flooded fields. Payable in pepper at harvest.",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": [
    "revathi"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-19-panel-01",
   "balloon": 2,
   "speakers": [
    "REVATHI"
   ],
   "text": "Today he speaks loudly about loyalty. When they come to collect, I wonder whose banner he will stand under.",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": [
    "revathi"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-19-panel-02",
   "balloon": 1,
   "speakers": [
    "NAGOJI"
   ],
   "text": "And you? Under whose banner will you stand, when the king and the company pull in different directions?",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": [
    "nagoji"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-19-panel-03",
   "balloon": 1,
   "speakers": [
    "REVATHI"
   ],
   "text": "I stand under Velinadu's.",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": [
    "revathi"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-19-panel-03",
   "balloon": 2,
   "speakers": [
    "REVATHI"
   ],
   "text": "The others move around us and hope we do not notice when they step on our toes.",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": [
    "revathi"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-20-panel-01",
   "balloon": 1,
   "speakers": [
    "RAMAYYAN"
   ],
   "text": "This is Karl August. He once wore the company's blue coat.",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": [
    "karl",
    "nagoji",
    "ramayyan"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-20-panel-01",
   "balloon": 2,
   "speakers": [
    "RAMAYYAN"
   ],
   "text": "Now he wears ours, when he wears anything at all.",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": [
    "karl",
    "nagoji",
    "ramayyan"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-20-panel-02",
   "balloon": 1,
   "speakers": [
    "KARL AUGUST"
   ],
   "text": "I fought for the Dutch. They did not pay. They did not feed. They left us to rot in mud and fever.",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": [
    "karl"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-20-panel-02",
   "balloon": 2,
   "speakers": [
    "KARL AUGUST"
   ],
   "text": "I decided I preferred to rot on my own terms.",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": [
    "karl"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-20-panel-03",
   "balloon": 1,
   "speakers": [
    "KARL AUGUST (off)"
   ],
   "text": "Colachel. Mud fort, half fallen. Powder and rice, too close together.",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": [
    "karl"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-20-panel-03",
   "balloon": 2,
   "speakers": [
    "KARL AUGUST (off)"
   ],
   "text": "They keep them in their little church. Stone keeps damp out better than canvas.",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": [
    "karl"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-20-panel-04",
   "balloon": 1,
   "speakers": [
    "KARL AUGUST"
   ],
   "text": "Kanyakumari camp. Men sick. Smallpox. No pay.",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": [
    "karl"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-20-panel-04",
   "balloon": 2,
   "speakers": [
    "KARL AUGUST"
   ],
   "text": "They hate their officers more than you do.",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": [
    "karl"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-20-panel-05",
   "balloon": 1,
   "speakers": [
    "RAMAYYAN"
   ],
   "text": "We will not win this war with bravery alone.",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": [
    "ramayyan"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-20-panel-05",
   "balloon": 2,
   "speakers": [
    "RAMAYYAN"
   ],
   "text": "We will win it with men who know where the enemy keeps his fire and his food.",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": [
    "ramayyan"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-21-panel-04",
   "balloon": 1,
   "speakers": [
    "IBRAHIM"
   ],
   "text": "He is just a man. He will bleed like any other if you cut him.",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": [
    "ibrahim",
    "nagoji",
    "kayal"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-21-panel-04",
   "balloon": 2,
   "speakers": [
    "NAGOJI"
   ],
   "text": "Until I see him on land, it is hard not to think of him as part of the ship.",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": [
    "ibrahim",
    "nagoji",
    "kayal"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-21-panel-05",
   "balloon": 1,
   "speakers": [
    "IBRAHIM"
   ],
   "text": "Then imagine him drowning. That will help.",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": [
    "ibrahim"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-22-panel-02",
   "balloon": 1,
   "speakers": [
    "IBRAHIM (off)"
   ],
   "text": "The tall one will note that your riders do not panic when the waves reach their hooves.",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": []
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-22-panel-02",
   "balloon": 2,
   "speakers": [
    "IBRAHIM (off)"
   ],
   "text": "Somewhere, a man with a powdered wig will tap that line and frown.",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": []
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-22-panel-03",
   "balloon": 1,
   "speakers": [
    "NAGOJI"
   ],
   "text": "Good. Let his wig itch.",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": [
    "ibrahim",
    "nagoji",
    "kayal"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-22-panel-03",
   "balloon": 2,
   "speakers": [
    "IBRAHIM"
   ],
   "text": "I should ride ahead. There are men in Kollam with contracts on both sides.",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": [
    "ibrahim",
    "nagoji",
    "kayal"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-22-panel-03",
   "balloon": 3,
   "speakers": [
    "NAGOJI"
   ],
   "text": "Both sides?",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": [
    "ibrahim",
    "nagoji",
    "kayal"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-22-panel-04",
   "balloon": 1,
   "speakers": [
    "IBRAHIM"
   ],
   "text": "I sell to whoever keeps this coast free enough for men like me to keep selling.",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": [
    "ibrahim"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-22-panel-04",
   "balloon": 2,
   "speakers": [
    "IBRAHIM"
   ],
   "text": "Today, that is your king.",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": [
    "ibrahim"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-22-panel-05",
   "balloon": 1,
   "speakers": [
    "IBRAHIM"
   ],
   "text": "Tomorrow? The sea does not care about flags. Neither do I.",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": [
    "ibrahim",
    "nagoji",
    "kayal"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-23-panel-01",
   "balloon": 1,
   "speakers": [
    "RAMAYYAN"
   ],
   "text": "The Dutch left angry. They know the King is shifting the pepper trade to the Syrian Christians. Tharakan and his kin.",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": [
    "nagoji",
    "ramayyan"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-23-panel-01",
   "balloon": 2,
   "speakers": [
    "NAGOJI"
   ],
   "text": "And the other chiefs?",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": [
    "nagoji",
    "ramayyan"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-23-panel-02",
   "balloon": 1,
   "speakers": [
    "RAMAYYAN"
   ],
   "text": "They grumble. Houses like Elayadathu prefer the Portuguese or the Dutch. They think white skin means heavier gold.",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": [
    "ramayyan"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-23-panel-02",
   "balloon": 2,
   "speakers": [
    "NAGOJI"
   ],
   "text": "Why not his own kind? Are there no Hindu merchants?",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": [
    "ramayyan"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-23-panel-03",
   "balloon": 1,
   "speakers": [
    "RAMAYYAN"
   ],
   "text": "You are from the Deccan, Sawant. For a Hindu of good caste to cross the black water is to lose his caste.",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": [
    "ramayyan"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-23-panel-03",
   "balloon": 2,
   "speakers": [
    "RAMAYYAN"
   ],
   "text": "The ocean is kalapani.",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": [
    "ramayyan"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-23-panel-04",
   "balloon": 1,
   "speakers": [
    "RAMAYYAN (off)"
   ],
   "text": "We can farm the pepper. We can tax the pepper. We cannot sail with it. That sin we leave to others.",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": [
    "ramayyan"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-23-panel-05",
   "balloon": 1,
   "speakers": [
    "NAGOJI"
   ],
   "text": "And the English at Anchuthengu?",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": [
    "nagoji",
    "ramayyan"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-23-panel-05",
   "balloon": 2,
   "speakers": [
    "RAMAYYAN"
   ],
   "text": "A Company doctor there lent us coin against Chanda Sahib. They call it a loan. We call it buying time.",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": [
    "nagoji",
    "ramayyan"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-23-panel-05",
   "balloon": 3,
   "speakers": [
    "NAGOJI"
   ],
   "text": "You trust him?",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": [
    "nagoji",
    "ramayyan"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-23-panel-05",
   "balloon": 4,
   "speakers": [
    "RAMAYYAN"
   ],
   "text": "I trust his fear.",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": [
    "nagoji",
    "ramayyan"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-24-panel-03",
   "balloon": 1,
   "speakers": [
    "NAGOJI (quiet)"
   ],
   "text": "Come closer. Come stand where I can reach you.",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": [
    "nagoji"
   ]
  },
  {
   "panel": "page-24-panel-03",
   "balloon": 2,
   "speakers": [
    "NAGOJI (quiet)"
   ],
   "text": "Let us see how your neat lines fare when the ground shifts under you.",
   "tail": "tail ringed",
   "cast": [
    "nagoji"
   ]
  }
 ]
}